CEO Dunhilton's Office, Government Tower, 0900 hours
\f1\i0 \
Dunhilton's office occupies the entire 73rd floor of the Government Tower, decorated in what interior designers refer to as "Megalomaniac Modern." The ceiling features a painted mural of Dunhilton as a Greek god, reclining on clouds while lesser deities (bearing suspicious resemblances to opposition politicians) grovel beneath him.\
Dunhilton doesn't look up from his desk as Jones enters. "You're the agent who got his arse handed to him by the Elvis impersonators, aren't you? You\'92re that Agent Jones? The one and the same?\'94\
Jones stands at rigid attention, a muscle in his jaw twitching. "There were unforeseen complications, sir."\
"Yes, you being utterly useless was quite unforeseen." Dunhilton finally raises his eyes, which resemble those of a predatory reptile contemplating whether to eat something now or save it for later. "Fortunately for you, I need someone expendable for a critical mission."\
Jones chooses to focus on "critical" rather than "expendable."\
Dunhilton slides a folder across his desk. "Sublime Point has become a problem. My intel suggests that Eloise Shakti is harboring something that could change the balance of power forever. We've discovered evidence of temporal anomalies, dimensional breaches\'97science fiction nonsense that my advisors assure me is actually happening."\
Jones flips through the folder, seeing surveillance photos of Sarah Jacobson with her enormous pregnant belly, schematics of the Gyges Disc experiments, and a grainy image of what appears to be a tear in reality itself.\
"I'm mobilizing all available forces for a direct assault on Sublime Point," Dunhilton continues. "But before that happens, I need someone on the inside. Someone to locate and eliminate one particular target."\
He slides another photo across the desk. It shows Gerry Hardman, aka "Jihad Man," conferring with Eloise Shakti in what appears to be a secured laboratory.\
Jones's heart rate increases. "Hardman."\
"I've suspected for some time that our Commissioner of Police is playing a deeper game," Dunhilton says. "And now we have proof he's in bed with Shakti Industries. I want him eliminated before he can implement whatever plan they've concocted."\
"It would be my genuine pleasure, sir." Jones practically salivates at the opportunity.\
Dunhilton narrows his eyes. "This is a precision operation. You'll infiltrate Sublime Point twelve hours before the main assault, locate Hardman, and neutralize him. Then you'll remain in place to open access points for my forces."\
"Understood, sir. When do I leave?"\
"You have seventy-two hours to prepare. My sources tell me the temporal anomalies will reach critical mass at midnight on December 25th. We strike just before then."\
As Jones turns to leave, Dunhilton adds, "Oh, and Jones? I understand that during the wedding reception evacuation, you were particularly rough with Dr. Smythe's unconscious body."\
Jones freezes. "Sir?"\
"Good instincts. The man's a radical and a troublemaker. Keep an eye out for him at Sublime Point. If you see him, feel free to finish what you started."\
Jones nods, unable to suppress a slight smile as he exits, already planning his revenge against both Hardman and Smythe. The gospel music incident already feels distant, a momentary weakness overcome.\
In the elevator down, he catches himself humming again and viciously bites the inside of his cheek until he tastes blood.\
